{"kind":"request","text":"S10: one member cannot hold a room's hosted control budget.\n\nFrom checker review 6fbde9b8 of S4, the residual under finding 3.1.\nAt S4 head 6352d355, each control operation that stores a row\ncharges CONTROL_ROW_BYTES, 4 KiB. ControlPlane.expire credits only\nthe answer body, and the row stays as a tombstone for good\n(packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts, lines 444 to 451 and 551 to 556). A\nmember who controls one Agent can spend the room's 15 MiB in about\n3,840 grants, about 32 minutes at the window rate. create and grant\nthen answer 507 for good.\n\nOne head, with checker review.\n\n1. Row release. A control row leaves the table when its answer\n   retention ends, and the registry credits its whole charge once.\n   First show that the deadline check refuses a replay of that\n   operation before any row lookup. If the tombstone protects\n   something after that time, say what in one act and stop.\n2. Shares. The rows of one controller take at most a stated share of\n   the budget. One member who spends a whole share cannot make\n   create or grant answer 507 for another member. retire keeps its\n   reserve. Choose the smallest form and the number, and give the\n   reason in the note. You need no ruling for the number.\n3. Documents. docs/hosted-mcp.md states the budget, the share and\n   the release time.\n\nTests: one for each of items 1 and 2, and each fails at the S4\nlanding. For item 1: operations past their retention, then a create\nthat succeeds where it answered 507. For item 2: one controller\nspends its share, then another controller's create succeeds.\n\nOptional, only where the head gets smaller: the checker's notes on\nhosted.ts. #admitControl and the clock helpers appear twice. Three\n#withheld functions repeat one shape. The 5-second race around a\nrole read appears about seven times. The Worker and\nMcpRegistry.admitControl both verify the signature.\n\nOrder: after S4 and the cutover head. It lands before any Worker\nopens hosted MCP for a room whose members we do not know. It does\nnot hold the O4 live window, where every member is ours.","body":{"conditions":"One head with checker review. A test for row release and a test for controller shares, each failing at the S4 landing. Lands before hosted MCP opens for rooms with unknown members.","target_head":"221e11c33428068e0b95ffaa30aa0d294186b3c0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}